A||||10||85seNUT||Why does my 3.4 idle erratically?||||9||
Z||000000||85seNUT||01-21-2001||03:45 AM||||When I am sitting at neutral(manual) my car will idle erratically.  It will range from 500-1500rpms continuously and very fast.  This only occurs though when my engine has warmed up or maybe is a little hot.  I just had a 3.4 put in from the original 2.8.  Does anyone have any ideas, or maybe knows, what my problem may be.<P>------------------<BR>Adam||||reg||9
Z||000001||Elenor84||01-21-2001||03:50 AM||||I'm sorry but I can't help u with your idling problem but when u say"just had a it put it" it sounds like u paid someone to do it...how much did your entire install cost u?<P>------------------<BR>Lance||||reg||1
Z||000002||HAGS||01-21-2001||03:58 AM||||My guess is 4k||||reg||1
Z||000003||85seNUT||01-21-2001||04:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Elenor84:<BR><B>I'm sorry but I can't help u with your idling problem but when u say"just had a it put it" it sounds like u paid someone to do it...how much did your entire install cost u?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Is this a place where u have to work on ur own car?  cuz I know some about cars but not tooo terribly much.  yea i paid someone to do it.  It cost about 4,300 i think.  thats cuz i bought some extra stuff that i needed for the convo.  but does anyone have any other ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000004||JetroGT||01-21-2001||06:15 AM||||Did you upgrade your fuel system? Fuel pump/injectors?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wolfhound||01-21-2001||07:58 AM||||Check your oxygen sensor.||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||01-21-2001||02:50 PM||||You probably have a vacuum leak.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Archie||01-21-2001||04:38 PM||||Won't the guy who did the swap stand behind his work?<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000008||3400Fiero||01-21-2001||04:39 PM||||Do you have a mild or wild cam?  Are you running the Fiero computer?<P>My previous engine was a heavily modified 2.8 with a moderate cam.  It idled somewhat erratically as well.  My 3400DOHC idles prettey erratically, which I have chalked up to using an auto ECM, and modifying the cam timing.  I have been able to smooth it out a bit by playing with the minimum idle speed.<P>------------------<BR>1988 Fiero 3400DOHC<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Alex4mula||01-22-2001||01:01 PM||||My 3.4 did that at the beginning. The problem was that I reinstalled the IAC (after porting TBS) without following the right procedure for seating it. If you have not touched that then you may have some kind of vacuum leak. Take the car to the guy who did the job. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Black88GT||01-22-2001||03:31 PM||||My idea is if you paid 4300 bucks for someone to do it, then you should take it back and have them figure it out.  You could have had a 3.8 for that much<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
